      "title": "Domino Players Student Costume Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPosition Summary: We are looking for Costume Design Majors to work in the costume shop as Costume Technicians. This position involves patternmaking, draping and sewing costumes with special skills in corsetry and tailoring. Essential Job Functions: Organizing the costume storage and shop. There are times student workers will be asked to work backstage as wardrobe crew during shows and to assist with wardrobe duties which include repairs and laundry. Maintenance of the Costume Shop sewing supplies and sewing machines is included in the daily responsibilities of the worker. Work Environment: The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those encountered while performing the essential functions of this job. The individual is routinely exposed to indoor conditions, minimum outdoor weather and temperature extremes, and moderate noise level. Qualifications/Prerequisites: SKILLS Ability to do basic sewing Experience in patternmaking, draping and skills in corsetry is not necessary, but will be learned on the job. EMPLOYMENT EXPERIENCE N/A EDUCATION Costume Design Major",
      "department": ""
