    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=537559482_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Head Women's Lacrosse Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-28\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nAlbright College is seeking applications for the Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach. This role is responsible for managing all aspects of the Women’s Lacrosse Program.  This includes the recruitment and management of a coaching staff, recruitment and retention of academically and athletically qualified student-athletes, and successful preparation, planning, and strategy for the development and sustaining of a highly competitive intercollegiate lacrosse program.  Additionally, the head coach needs to be involved in fund raising and other duties as assigned.  There will be a secondary duty. Essential Job Functions: 1. Lead the women’s lacrosse program with on field coaching.  2. Supervise and professionally develop assistant coaches. 3. Recruit prospective student athletes on and off campus. Evaluate player talent for recruits.  4. Organize recruiting communications and campus visits.  5. Set up and monitor student athlete academics.  6. Lead retention efforts for lacrosse players.  7. Game preparation and strategy.  8. Attend all MAC women’s lacrosse coach meetings.  9. Organize program fundraising.  10. Maintain team social media pages.  11. Promote diverse and inclusive atmosphere within the program.  12  Active involvement in fundraising related to women’s lacrosse. 13. Active engagement of women’s lacrosse alums. 14. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications/Prerequisites: COMMUNICATION Strong communication skills with a demonstrated ability in leading and mentoring. SKILLS Fluency in Spanish, preferred. EMPLOYMENT EXPERIENCE Minimum of five years of progressive college coaching experience Head coaching experience preferred. EDUCATION Bachelor’s degree required, Master’s degree preferred Review of applications for this position will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants should complete an application by clicking “Apply Now”.  Cover letter, a minimum of two professional references and any other supporting application materials can be uploaded in one document along with the resume.  Optional documents may be submitted can include: proof of education/certification, licenses, and letters of recommendation.  Albright offers a competitive benefits package, which includes tuition remission.  Albright offers a competitive benefits package, which includes tuition remission.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=537533033_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Peer Tutor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-28\n\nPosition Summary: Peer Tutors are academic student leaders who play an important role in supporting the Albright community. They help motivate and encourage students in their learning while providing academic support tailored to individual course needs. As members of the Peer Tutoring staff, tutors work with students through our CircleIn AI tutoring system, one-on-one, and in small-group sessions to review course material and strengthen academic skills. Tutoring responsibilities may include, but are not limited to: Supporting students through the writing process, including brainstorming, outlining, drafting, revising, and editing Answering questions and providing clarification on course content Reviewing course material and providing constructive feedback Helping students develop effective study strategies and create study materials Providing practice and preparation opportunities to reinforce mastery of course content Helping students develop general academic and study skills Peer Tutors work approximately 5 hours per week, with schedules based on student and program needs. Additional responsibilities may include leading class visits, helping design and present academic workshops, tabling at admissions events, and assisting with special programs and events. This is a great opportunity for students who enjoy working with their peers and are organized, patient, approachable, and comfortable greeting others and presenting information. Peer Tutors should be enthusiastic about helping fellow students succeed and committed to creating a welcoming and supportive learning environment. Essential Job Functions Complete required training by established deadlines Commit to at least 5 hours per week of tutoring throughout the semester Check email daily and communicate with tutees as needed Complete accurate and timely tutoring session summaries Communicate with professors or supervisors about student progress when requested Participate in semester self-evaluations Follow Student Academic Support and College policies and uphold the College’s values and expectations Qualifications & Requirements Strong academic performance and demonstrated mastery of the subject(s) tutored Reliable, flexible, and able to manage scheduling and email communication effectively Strong written and verbal communication skills Empathetic, approachable, and able to support students experiencing academic challenges Ability to maintain student confidentiality For Writing Support Tutors: strong writing skills, including brainstorming, drafting, revision/editing, research, and citation Experience Peer Tutors are selected based on academic ability, leadership, character, communication skills, and subject expertise. Tutors should be able to effectively communicate course content and support their peers' learning. Education Earned a B+ or higher in the course(s) they wish to tutor Faculty recommendation from the instructor(s) of the course(s) they wish to tutor Applicants will be asked to contact their professor(s) to complete the Faculty Recommendation Form",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=537500865_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Sports Information Student Worker",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-28\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPosition Summary: This position will help create an atmosphere aligning with the Athletic Department mission to represent, promote and maintain data for athletes from all demographics. Albright is an NCAA Division III member institution as well as a member of the Middle Atlantic Conference (MAC), and the Commonwealth Conference. For this student worker position, the student worker will assist the sports information director & the assistant sports information director, with day-to-day operations of the program. The chosen candidate will also share in social media and webcasting responsibilities and other duties assigned by director.   Essential Job Functions: Assist director with day to day operations. Maintain Albright Athletics Social Media Sites (Twitter, Facebook, Instagram) Design Game programs Write press releases/game recaps Maintain team statistics Compile statistics using Statcrew/NCAA Genius software program Design graphics for social media use   Qualifications/Prerequisites: SKILLS a. Flexibility b. Some computer skills c. Willingness to learn EMPLOYMENT EXPERIENCE a. Some experience working similar position is an advantage. Persons with little or no of experience will be considered if willing to learn. EDUCATION a. Student in good standing at Albright College",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=537194955_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct of Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPosition Summary:  Albright College’s Chemistry program in the Division of Natural Sciences seeks applications for adjunct faculty to teach laboratory. Successful candidates will teach a section of General Chemistry I and/or Organic Chemistry I laboratory for Fall 2026, and opportunities exist for future teaching. Laboratory sections are in-person for 3.5 hours on the Albright campus in Reading, PA. The laboratory curriculum is shared across all sections of the laboratory course, including common learning objectives, procedures, safety protocols, and grading procedures. The successful candidate will join a dynamic department committed to excellence in teaching and will support the College’s mission of enabling students to live their best lives, now and in the future. The College is consistently named as a top performer in social mobility and in return on investment.  Required Qualification: MS or PhD in chemistry, biochemistry, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with teaching undergraduate students and/or assisting with laboratories. Experience with a learning management system such as Brightspace. Essential Job Duties A successful candidate will: Provide background for laboratory experiments to General Chemistry and/or Organic Chemistry laboratory sections, ensuring students grasp fundamental concepts and develop essential laboratory skills. Aid students during laboratory sessions. Maintain and organize laboratory equipment and supplies. Evaluate student performance with timely and constructive feedback using common evaluation procedures across sections. Enforce laboratory safety protocols and hazardous waste procedures. Respond to student questions during office hours and by email throughout the semester. For further information, contact the Chair of the Natural Sciences, Dr. Ian Rhile at irhile@albright.edu . Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter addressing qualifications Curriculum vitae or resume The names and contact information for two references Review of applications for the position will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants should complete an application by clicking “Apply Now.” Optional documents may be submitted such as evidence of education or previous teaching effectiveness.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=536725008_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Career Center Ambassador",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPosition Summary: Responsible for assisting with the CDC’s daily operations. Essential Job Functions: Act as a resource for Albright faculty, staff, and students, as well as external partners such as employers, via telephone, email, in person, and through the Handshake platform Respond to information requests from students, employers, community members, and other educational institutions Work collaboratively with other departments to assist with events hosted by the CDC ( Career & Internship Fair/Tabling Event/Professional Development Workshops. Assist with Handshake and Focus2 platform Update the CDC web pages, social media, and Handshake calendars and events Assist with the Career Closet donations and ensure students have access to professional attire Perform other tasks according to departmental needs and the mission of the college Qualifications/Prerequisites: 1. COMMUNICATION Excellent communication skills, written and verbal, including the ability to deal tactfully with different audiences 2. SKILLS a. Confidentiality b. Knowledge of resume, cover letter, job/internship search, etc. c. Ability to multitask d. Problem-solving and decision-making skills e. Organizational skills f. Team player with the ability to work independently g. Quick learner; committed to efficiency and accuracy with attention to detail h. Knowledge of Handshake, TimelyCare, Instagram, Microsoft 356, Word, Excel, Outlook",
